We can take it for granted that c events in Gehennom are mostly
plain operator mishaps with their corpse. If you are not confident
that you learn how to handle them you probably should just put the
corpses in your bag - as frightened people suggested in the past -
until the corpse rots away, instead of wasting a precious scroll
which is better applied on any of the many active threats.

Your comparison with the Wizard is not very helpful, I think; the
Wizard will only appear a few times and very very late in the game.
The Wizard is also very tough that one is usally spending charges
of a wand of death, which means instant death for him; rarely you'd
do that with a cockatrice.

For folks who want to keep the cockatrices alive to use them as a
instant weapon, e.g. against the Wizard; just wield it as secondary
weapon and always do the three keys 'x' '<direction>' 'x' as action
against the foes. A fast, simple, and timely uncritical procedure
to be (fairly ;-) save.

